WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.190
What’s the easternmost point in the US?

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:10.219
Well it’s actually a more complicated question
than you may think.

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:12.050
The simple answer would be Maine.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:16.099
Sail Rock, Maine to be specific, and if you
said this answer you would be right, but only

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:18.780
in one way of looking at the easternmost point.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:23.080
This is only right if you think of the easternmost
point in the United States as relative to

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.130
the United States itself and looking at the
US as only the 50 states of the US, but you

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.850
have to remember the overseas territories
of the US.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:34.680
In this case, if we include the territories
of the US, not including embassies, bases,

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.840
or war cemeteries which are technically US
soil but not US territories, the easternmost

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.710
point in the US, relative to the mainland
United States would be Point Udall, in the

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.400
US Virgin Islands.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.610
Interestingly, the westernmost point of the
United States relative to the United States

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:55.570
is also named Point Udall, this time in Guam,
but thats a topic for another time.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:01:00.409
So these easternmost points are all talking
about east relative to the US, but we must

00:01:00.409 --> 00:01:02.909
remember that that’s not really what east
is.

00:01:02.909 --> 00:01:07.630
“East” is a relative term, and in it’s
true sense, it’s all about longitude.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:12.530
“East” essentially means to the right
of the prime meridian line, while “west”

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:13.530
is to the left.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.799
So when we look at Alaska, which includes
a long line of islands called the Aleutian

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:23.100
Islands, we see that what was west eventually
becomes east because this island chain actually

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:28.670
crosses the 180th line of longitude, the exact
opposite of the prime meridian.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:33.940
Therefore the closest island to the west of
the prime meridian, Semisopochnoi Island,

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:38.150
holds the title of being the easternmost point
in the United States.

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:42.020
Now this creates a very interesting paradox
where the easternmost point in the United

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:46.679
States is actually west, in terms of direction
of travel, of the westernmost point of the

00:01:46.679 --> 00:01:51.500
US, Amatignak Island, by about 30 miles.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.720
This is of course assuming that you are looking
at the westernmost and easternmost point in

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.850
terms of longitude.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:03.049
Now to finish off, this creates one more paradox
where Alaska holds the title of being the

00:02:03.049 --> 00:02:08.590
northernmost, westernmost, and easternmost
state all at the same time.

